# TRIAD asynchronous-planner source synchronization manifest
#
# The implementation files listed below were synchronized directly from the
# frozen scientific development state f56add3 in the TRIAD development
# repository. That state is the head of the following lineage, in which the
# complete finite search was progressively isolated from the mc_rtc control
# callback and finally moved onto one background worker:
#
#   route certification made resumable (one route per cycle)
#   predictive route rollout made resumable (bounded work units)
#   live-robot reads removed from the copied-state rollout
#   planner data boundary: PlanningSnapshot, PlannerContext, FrozenPlanSet
#   planner configuration frozen behind PlannerConfig
#   complete finite search isolated from the FSM
#   search given its own planner-owned world
#   search moved onto one background worker
#   commit freshness recorded; verbose evidence made switchable
#   perception-latency configuration read corrected
#
# No scientific parameter was changed at any point in that lineage: the preview
# integration step, the event, grasp and route banks, hard feasibility,
# J_global, the objective weights, the timing thresholds, the tie rules and the
# one-commit / no-replanning semantics are untouched throughout. The only
# configuration addition is routeWorkUnitsPerCycle, a work-unit scheduling
# budget that redistributes already-defined route work across control cycles.
#
# Equivalence evidence: the frozen plan sets of three of the four Dataset-B
# scenarios are byte-identical between the control-thread and worker builds at
# 17 significant digits; the fourth is a strict superset that additionally
# enumerates one event hypothesis which the wall-clock-dependent elapsed-lead
# prune had skipped before its geometry ran.
#
# This publication commit is not the same commit as f56add3. It is a curated
# publication commit whose implementation files are byte-identical to that
# frozen development state.
#
# Verify with:
#   sha256sum -c docs/source_sync_f56add3.sha256
#
# Columns: <sha256>  <path>
